  "date": "07/09/2026",
  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Compatibility & Evolution",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What You May Change"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mode",
            "Allowed change"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`BACKWARD`",
              "delete a field"
            ],
            [
              "`BACKWARD`",
              "add a field WITH a default"
            ],
            [
              "`FORWARD`",
              "add a field"
            ],
            [
              "`FORWARD`",
              "delete a field that HAS a default"
            ],
            [
              "`FULL`",
              "add/remove optional-with-default only"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Never allowed (any non-NONE mode)",
          "items": [
            "Renaming a field without an alias",
            "`string` → `int` and other incompatible retypes",
            "Removing an enum symbol under forward compat"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Safe Moves"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "{\"name\":\"email\",\"aliases\":[\"mail\"],",
            " \"type\":[\"null\",\"string\"],",
            " \"default\":null}   # the optional idiom",
            "// bare \"string\" with no default: unremovable"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Aliases are the only safe rename — the reader maps old name to new",
            "Avro promotes `int → long → float → double`, and `string ⇄ bytes`",
            "Narrowing is never safe, in either direction",
            "New enum symbol breaks forward compat unless the enum has a `default` (Avro 1.9+)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Pick By Lifetime"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Match mode to retention",
          "text": "Compacted or infinite-retention topics keep ancient data alive, so they need `*_TRANSITIVE`. Short-retention event streams are fine on plain `BACKWARD`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What An SMT Is",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Per-record, in-process, between connector and converter",
            "No external system, no state, no joins",
            "Configured, not coded — it lives in the connector JSON"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Order Matters"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "compare",
          "spec": {
            "left": {
              "title": "Source order",
              "items": [
                "connector",
                "SMT chain",
                "converter",
                "Kafka"
              ]
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "Sink order",
              "items": [
                "Kafka",
                "converter",
                "SMT chain",
                "connector"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "properties",
          "lines": [
            "transforms=unwrap,route",
            "transforms.unwrap.type=io.deb...ExtractNewRecordState",
            "transforms.unwrap.delete.handling.mode=rewrite",
            "transforms.route.type=org...RegexRouter",
            "transforms.route.replacement=app_$1  # named steps"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "SMTs & Predicates",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Working Set"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "SMT",
            "Does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`InsertField`",
              "add static/topic/offset/ts"
            ],
            [
              "`ExtractField$Key`",
              "field becomes the whole key"
            ],
            [
              "`ValueToKey`",
              "copy value fields into key"
            ],
            [
              "`ReplaceField`",
              "include, exclude, rename"
            ],
            [
              "`MaskField`",
              "redact PII in place"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Cast` retypes a field; `TimestampConverter` moves string ⇄ epoch ⇄ Date",
            "`RegexRouter` rewrites the topic via `regex` + `replacement` — the prefix stripper",
            "`Flatten` collapses nested Structs to `parent.child` so JDBC can write them",
            "`ValueToKey` + `ExtractField$Key` is the standard way to key a CDC stream by PK"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Predicates"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "properties",
          "lines": [
            "predicates=isDead",
            "predicates.isDead.type=...RecordIsTombstone",
            "transforms.x.predicate=isDead",
            "transforms.x.negate=true   # skip tombstones"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Built-ins: `TopicNameMatches`, `HasHeaderKey`, `RecordIsTombstone`",
            "`negate=true` inverts any of them",
            "A predicate gates one SMT, not the whole chain"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Limits"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Hard no",
          "items": [
            "No aggregation, no cross-record joins",
            "No external lookups",
            "No splitting one record into many"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "SMTs rewrite the schema too",
          "text": "The transformed schema is the one registered, so adding an SMT can trip a compatibility check. Each SMT also costs a per-record allocation — past ~5 steps, move the work to Kafka Streams."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Config Mistakes",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Internal topics at RF=1 — one broker loss erases configs and offsets",
            "`schemas.enable=true` at volume: 3-5× storage and network, zero governance",
            "`tasks.max=20` on a single-table JDBC or single-binlog Debezium — still 1 task",
            "`auto.register.schemas=true` in prod lets a rogue deploy poison a subject"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Runtime Mistakes"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Symptom",
            "Real cause"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Unknown magic byte!`",
              "converter mismatch"
            ],
            [
              "JSON parse error",
              "same, other direction"
            ],
            [
              "Full re-snapshot",
              "renamed connector / prefix"
            ],
            [
              "Consumer can't decode",
              "hard-deleted schema version"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Failure Modes & Ops",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Mismatched converters surface as byte errors, never as schema errors",
            "Changing `topic.prefix` or `database.server.name` re-snapshots too",
            "No DLQ + `errors.tolerance=none` = one bad record halts everything at 3am",
            "DLQ configured but unmonitored = data quietly vanishing for weeks"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Diagnosis"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kafka-consumer-groups --describe \\",
            "  --group connect-s3-sink \\",
            "  --bootstrap-server b:9092",
            "# the status API does NOT show lag"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Alarm on these",
          "items": [
            "`connector-task-metrics.status`",
            "`sink-record-lag-max`",
            "`source-record-poll-rate`",
            "`deadletterqueue-produce-requests`, rebalance rate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Recovery Order"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "GET status",
              "read task trace",
              "fix config or record",
              "restart?includeTasks=true",
              "watch lag"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Offset Surgery"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "PUT /connectors/x/stop      # must be STOPPED",
            "GET /connectors/x/offsets   # inspect",
            "PATCH /connectors/x/offsets # rewind",
            "DELETE /connectors/x/offsets # wipe"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "This replaces the old hand-editing of the offsets topic",
            "Size workers by heap and network, not CPU",
            "Object-storage sinks need heap ≈ `flush.size` × record size",
            "Secrets via `config.providers` (`FileConfigProvider`, Vault) — never plaintext in the config topic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Connect is not exactly-once",
          "text": "Unless source EOS is explicitly enabled and the sink upserts idempotently, assume duplicates and design the target to absorb them."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Decision Table",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
