    {
      "page_title": "Design Decisions & Recap",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Decision",
            "Pick",
            "When"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Subject",
              "`TopicNameStrategy`",
              "one type per topic"
            ],
            [
              "Subject",
              "`TopicRecordName`",
              "ordered event union"
            ],
            [
              "Transform",
              "SMT",
              "field-level shaping"
            ],
            [
              "Transform",
              "Streams / Flink",
              "joins, aggregation, fan-out"
            ],
            [
              "Deploy",
              "distributed ≥3",
              "everything but edge/dev"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Trade-Offs"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Throughput vs latency: bigger batches, longer `flush.interval` — slower end-to-end, wider replay windows",
            "Availability vs correctness: `errors.tolerance=all` stays up but loses rows into the DLQ; `none` makes you notice",
            "Governance vs velocity: CI registration slows teams less than the outage it prevents"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Schemas Cost"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "~5 bytes per record for the magic byte and ID",
            "One cached HTTP lookup per new schema ID",
            "Negligible beside embedded-schema JSON"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Breaking Change Recipe"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "1 create orders.v2",
            "2 dual-write from the source",
            "3 migrate consumers, verify lag + counts",
            "4 retire v1  # never mutate past the mode"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Before You Deploy"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Checklist",
          "items": [
            "Converters agreed topic-wide; compatibility set per subject",
            "`tasks.max` matched to real parallelism",
            "DLQ topic created AND monitored",
            "Internal topics RF=3; secrets via config providers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "source",
              "connector + SMTs",
              "converter",
              "registry ID + bytes",
              "Kafka",
              "converter + SMTs",
              "sink"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Three rules to leave with",
          "text": "The converter is a topic-wide contract. Compatibility mode must match data lifetime. Every offset is keyed by connector name — so names are permanent."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Next: read the Debezium docs for your database",
            "Run `kafka-avro-console-consumer` on a real topic",
            "Script compatibility checks into CI"
          ]
        }
